course: dictionary
lesson: 1607
title: Cheerless and gloomy places
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words describe how a place feels, not just how it looks. Cheerless is one of them. It means gloomy, dull and without anything to make you happy or comfortable. Read the words around it to find the clues.
explain: In «the cheerless, deserted look of the long-neglected house», the clues are deserted and long-neglected. Nobody has cared for the house or lived in it for ages, so it feels grey and sad. Cheerless is describing the feeling of the place.
explain: Writers use cheerless for cold rooms, grey days and sad places. Mole's home is warm and bright, so it is the opposite of cheerless. When you meet a word like this, try swapping in your meaning: does «gloomy and without comfort» still make sense? If it does, you have it.
fact: Cheerless means gloomy, dull and without anything to make you happy or comfortable.
fact: «Cheerless» is an adjective, so it describes a noun, such as a room, a day or a house.
fact: The opposite of cheerless is cheerful, which means bright and happy.
fact: In «the cheerless, deserted look of the long-neglected house», the word cheerless describes how the house looks.
fact: Cheerless, gloomy and dull all describe a place without much light or comfort, but cheerless often suggests the place feels sad.
exercise: «The room was cold, grey and cheerless.» What does cheerless mean here? | Noisy and crowded with people | Bright, warm and full of music | Very tidy and freshly painted | *Gloomy and dull, with nothing to make you happy
exercise: «The dust lying thick on everything … the cheerless, deserted look of the long-neglected house». What is cheerless describing? | The Mole | The dust | *The look of the house | The size of the rooms
exercise: Which word is the opposite of cheerless? | Gloomy | Dull | *Cheerful | Grey
test: Which place would a writer most likely call cheerless? | A sunny garden full of flowers | *A cold, grey room with no light and no warmth | A warm kitchen with a crackling fire | A bright party full of music and laughter
test: The Mole sees the old house and calls it cheerless. What does this tell us? | It has just been painted and is very tidy | It is the warmest home in the wood | *It feels gloomy and without comfort | It is full of happy guests
exam: In «the cheerless, deserted look of the long-neglected house», what does cheerless mean? | Loud, busy and full of visitors | Freshly painted and very tidy | Warm, bright and welcoming | *Gloomy, dull and without anything to make you happy or comfortable
